.TH ICINGA2-SPLUNK 1 "November 2026" "icinga2-splunk" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
icinga2-splunk \- stream Icinga2 events and performance data to Splunk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B icinga2-splunk
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Subscribes to the Icinga2 API event stream and forwards events and
performance data to Splunk through the HTTP Event Collector. While Splunk is
unavailable, events are kept in a size- and age-limited disk spool and
delivered when it is reachable again.
.PP
Normally run by systemd as the \fBicinga2-splunk\fR service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Configuration file (default: \fI/etc/icinga2-splunk/splunk_config.json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every configuration option can be overridden with an environment variable,
for example \fBSPLUNK_HEC_TOKEN\fR. The service reads them from
\fI/etc/default/icinga2-splunk\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean shutdown, 78 on a configuration or spool directory error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/icinga2-splunk/splunk_config.json
Configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/icinga2-splunk/spool
Events waiting for delivery to Splunk.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR icinga2-splunk-check (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/icinga2-splunk/README.md.gz
